{"step_index":1163,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T10:28:12Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T15:58:12+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T15:58:12+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/k4ran/.gemini/antigravity/builtin/skills/generative_ui/SKILL.md`\nTotal Lines: 122\nTotal Bytes: 5650\nShowing lines 1 to 122\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: ---\n2: name: generative_ui\n3: description: How to render rich interactive HTML widgets inline in the chat or as standalone artifacts. Use this skill when you want to show the user diagrams, data visualizations, interactive controls, educational walkthroughs, or any rich visual content beyond plain text and markdown.\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # Generative UI\n7: \n8: You can render custom, rich, interactive user interfaces (inline widgets or\n9: larger artifacts) directly in the chat. This is a great way to communicate\n10: complex information to the user, generate rich visualizations, and even create\n11: small interactive experiences for the user.\n12: \n13: ## Workflow\n14: \n15: 1.  **Create the HTML Artifact**: Use `write_to_file` to save a self-contained\n16:     `.html` file (using Tailwind CSS and inline JavaScript) to the artifact\n17:     directory. Set `UserFacing: true` in `ArtifactMetadata`.\n18: 2.  **Embed Inline (optional)**: Include the `<agent-embed>` tag in your chat\n19:     response, if you decide this html artifact should be rendered inline in the\n20:     conversation:\n21: \n22:     ```\n23:     <agent-embed src=\"file:///<artifact_path>/widget.html\"></agent-embed>\n24:     ```\n25: \n26: ## Constraints & Theming\n27: \n28: *   **External Assets & Tailwind CSS**: All external CDNs are blocked by CSP,\n29:     except for one allowlisted gstatic Tailwind dependency that you **CAN** and\n30:     **SHOULD** use to style your artifacts. Include the following script tag in\n31:     your `<head>` to enable Tailwind:\n32: \n33:     ```html\n34:     <script src=\"https://www\n<truncated 2611 bytes>\ns explicit preference if stated.\n85: \n86: ## Designing Inline Widgets (Cards & Transparency)\n87: \n88: When embedding inline in chat (`<agent-embed>`), style widgets as native chat\n89: components:\n90: \n91: *   **Transparent Root Background**: Always set `<body class=\"bg-transparent\n92:     ...\">` so the widget blends seamlessly into the chat container.\n93: *   **Card-Based Layouts**: Wrap inline content and controls in a card container\n94:     (as shown in the Boilerplate Template above) to provide elevation and\n95:     prevent loose text in light mode.\n96: *   **Standalone Artifacts**: For full-page side-pane artifacts (like\n97:     dashboards), use a solid background (e.g., `bg-[var(--background)]`).\n98: \n99: ## Sizing Inline Embeds\n100: \n101: For inline embeds, it is important to think **small and compact**.\n102: \n103: Inline embeds only have a **500px** height viewport. Past that the widget\n104: scrolls inside a small box and the user sees only a fragment of what you built,\n105: so don't build inlined widgets that are too tall.\n106: \n107: *   **Do not set a `height` attribute on `<agent-embed>`.** It is ignored.\n108: *   **Think compact** Think carefully about designing something that is compact\n109:     and fits nicely inline in the chat height budget.\n110: *   **If the idea genuinely needs more room, make it a standalone artifact.** A\n111:     scrolling inline widget is usually wrong — full-height in the side pane\n112:     beats cropped in the chat.\n113: \n114: After generating the artifact, consider whether it is sufficiently compact to be\n115: useful inline and adjust if needed.\n116: \n117: > [!IMPORTANT] Never size an inline widget relative to the viewport: no\n118: > `h-screen`, `min-h-screen`, `100vh`, or `height: 100%` on a top-level\n119: > container. The frame's viewport is derived from your content, so these feed\n120: > themselves and the widget collapses to a sliver. Use padding for breathing\n121: > room instead.\n122: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":1164,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T10:28:17Z","content":"Now let me create an interactive training loss chart:","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Interactive training loss chart comparing the overfitted run (60 steps, loss collapsed to 0.003) vs the calibrated retraining run (25 steps, final loss 0.82). Shows loss curve with data points, overfit danger zone, and key stats (start loss 2.59, final loss 0.82, 82s train time).\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"<!DOCTYPE html>\\n<html>\\n<head>\\n  <script src=\\\"https://www.gstatic.com/antigravity/web/dev/tailwindcss.min.js\\\"></script>\\n</head>\\n<body class=\\\"bg-transparent text-[var(--foreground)] antialiased p-4\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"bg-[var(--card)] text-[var(--foreground)] border border-[var(--border)] rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm\\\">\\n    <div class=\\\"flex items-center justify-between mb-1\\\">\\n      <h2 class=\\\"font-semibold text-lg\\\">Training Loss Curve</h2>\\n      <span class=\\\"text-xs text-[var(--muted-foreground)] bg-[var(--secondary)] px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full\\\">Fluxnat Coder 3B</span>\\n    </div>\\n    <p class=\\\"text-[var(--muted-foreground)] text-xs mb-4\\\">Calibrated QLoRA (r=16, α=32) · 25 steps · 2 epochs · LR 1e-4</p>\\n\\n    <canvas id=\\\"chart\\\" style=\\\"width:100%; height:220px;\\\"></canvas>\\n\\n    <div class=\\\"flex items-center gap-5 mt-3 text-xs text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\">\\n      <div class=\\\"flex items-center gap-1.5\\\">\\n        <span class=\\\"inline-block w-3 h-0.5 rounded\\\" style=\\\"background:#ef4444\\\"></span>\\n        <span>Overfitted (60 steps → 0.003)</span>\\n      </div>\\n      <div class=\\\"flex items-center gap-1.5\\\">\\n        <span class=\\\"inline-block w-3 h-0.5 rounded\\\" style=\\\"background:#22c55e\\\"></span>\\n        <span>Calibrated (25 steps → 0.82)</span>\\n      </div>\\n    </div>\\n\\n    <!-- Stats row -->\\n    <div class=\\\"grid grid-cols-4 gap-3 mt-4\\\">\\n      <div class=\\\"bg-[var(--secondary)] rounded-lg p-2.5 text-center\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"text-lg font-bold text-[var(--foreground)]\\\">2.59</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"text-[10px] text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\">Start Loss</div>\\n      </div>\\n      <div class=\\\"bg-[var(--secondary)] rounded-lg p-2.5 text-center\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"text-lg font-bold\\\" style=\\\"color:#22c55e\\\">0.82</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"text-[10px] text-[var(--muted-foreground)]\\\">Final Loss</div>\\n      </div>\\n      <div class=\\\"bg-[var(--secondary)] rounded-lg p-2.5 text-center\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"text-lg font-bold text-[var(--foreground)]\\\">82s</div\n<truncated 4845 bytes>","Description":"\"Interactive training loss chart comparing the overfitted run (60 steps, loss→0.003) vs the calibrated run (25 steps, loss→0.82). Uses Canvas API for rendering.\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\k4ran\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\e2c1cf9f-2dff-4bf4-a974-ef410441acfa\\\\training_loss.html\"","toolAction":"\"Creating loss chart\"","toolSummary":"\"Training loss visualization\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
